    }
  },
  "rule": "Colour-0 rectangular frames sit on a non-zero background. Frame corners may carry a coloured marker on their inner diagonal at depth D. One corner (occasionally two) is already decorated with a small shape, and that shape is the template. In the output, the template is copied to every other marked corner. Each copy is mirrored to that corner's orientation and drawn in that corner's marker colour. Unmarked corners stay unchanged.",
  "scope": "Infer a decorated frame-corner template and mirror/recolour it into other marked corners, leaving unmarked corners unchanged. One to three optionally clipped zero-colour rectangular frames on backgrounds 1..9; requested canvas, template, depth and frame counts honored. Random templates diagonal-symmetric; caller-supplied asymmetric templates supported.",
  "constraints": [
    "Read saved repaired corner detector and candidate signature/window checks",
    "Require at least one visible decorated template in explicit mode",
    "120 targeted scenes cover 40 asymmetric templates, 40 three-frame depth-2 scenes and 40 depth-3 scenes on 13x13 canvases",
    "Each output equals the supplied template stamps at exactly the undeveloped marked corners; other cells unchanged",
    "Randomized one-frame fallback honors all requested geometry/palette/template controls; multi-frame requests fail rather than silently shrink"
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Decorations are confined to offsets [-2,3] and cover at most the first cell of each arm.",
    "Default depths are 1 or 2; depth 3 is opt-in.",
    "Default templates are diagonal-symmetric; asymmetric templates are explicit random controls only.",
    "Random marked-corner footprints do not clip; clipped frames contribute unmarked distractor corners.",
    "Overlapping/nested frames and more than two predecorated corners are absent."
  ],
